<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Best in Slot Gear list for Holy Paladin Healer in Cataclysm Classic Pre-Raid. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from dungeons, reputations, and professions. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">
<span class="c4">Best in Slot Gear for Holy Paladin Healer in Pre-Raid</span></h2>Holy Paladin sees a major itemization shift in Cataclysm due to the introduction of armor spec bonuses - a 5% bonus to your primary stat when you wear purely armor of your type. In our case, that means having to wear all plate - no more wearing cloth, leather, or mail for us. Additionally, all MP5 gets changed to Spirit and all healers really like Spirit now.<br/>
<br/>Due to reforging, most items are functionally very equivalent to each other as long as they're the same item level. Additionally, at the gear level of Tier 11/<wbr/>Phase 1 of Cataclysm, our overall stats are low enough that Intellect itself is extremely powerful compared to any secondary stat, meaning that differences between same-ilvl gear are very very minute.<br/>
<br/>What this means for our gearing strategy is that we will favor item level first. Due our overall low intellect at this ilvl, most secondaries are quite close - so while we do favor spirit and haste, item level will mean we wear non-spirit/<wbr/>haste gear at times.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Intellect - Intellect now directly provides spellpower, and spellpower can't be gemmed, meaning that we CONTINUE to gem Intellect as it also continues to provide mana and crit. However, Intellect is now a red gem.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Spirit - All healers in Cataclysm now use Spirit instead of MP5, even Paladins and Shaman. Getting a lot of Spirit is important for Holy Paladin as it's a very mana hungry spec, especially if casting <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=82327/holy-radiance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_paladin_divinecircle.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Holy Radiance</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - Haste continues to be a great throughput stat, but now that Holy Paladins no longer have infinite mana with Divine Plea, it's much less important until you start getting high levels of mana stats.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Mastery - Hey, remember Val'anyr? Now you get the effect on ALL of your heals, all the time, permanently! One big side effect is that the shield does not apply to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=53563/beacon-of-light">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_beaconoflight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Beacon of Light</span></a> healing, meaning that the 50% Beacon healing transfer is in actuality even lower due to no Mastery shield. Luckily in 4.2, Mastery shields were made able to fully stack and refresh themselves, so we have an ultra powerful version.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Critical Strike - Crit continues to be a lackluster stat, specifically due to how much stat rating 1% critical strike costs on gear.</div></li></ol>
<div style="text-align: -webkit-center;">
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="absolute-pre-raid-bis">Absolute Pre-Raid BiS</h4>This is the best possible setup you could have before stepping into a single raid in Phase 1. However, this setup is obviously incredibly unrealistic as it not only requires two extremely rare world drops, it also requires a lot of Valor to put together (not including the boots!) While this is an aspirational setup, it is not very realistic and is here solely as an informative display of what can be achieved with only non-raid gear.<br/>
<br/>
