<br/>
<br/>A quick note on tierset bonus, since we can achieve 3pc via Valor - the 2pc bonus is very weak, so it's not necessary to optimize tierset purchases especially if you are gearing up a new Holy Paladin later into the phase. Especially if you can purchase the BoE chest cheaply, that can be a much faster way of accomplishing a competent pre-raid setup prior to stepping into a raid.<br/>
<br/>Due to reforging, most items are functionally very equivalent to each other as long as they're the same item level. Additionally, at the gear level of Tier 11/<wbr/>Phase 1 of Cataclysm, our overall stats are low enough that Intellect itself is extremely powerful compared to any secondary stat, meaning that differences between same-ilvl gear are very very minute. For this reason, all 346s on this list have been listed in no particular order; instead, wherever listed, we have listed the secondary stats on the item so you can make a personal decision.<br/>
<br/>Overall, this means that for our gearing strategy, there isn't necessarily a single "best option" per item level if multiple items at the same ilvl exist. <b>For this reason, we have chosen to show all 346s in this list, with information on what secondaries they have.</b> As a simple reference, all "Best" items are 359 (with the exception of shoulder/<wbr/>wrists/<wbr/>weapon which have no 359 option), and all "Good" items are 346.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="justice-points">Justice Points for Holy Paladin Healer Pre-Raid</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a>s are one of the two new PvE currencies in Cataclysm (<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>s being the other one). They have a hard cap of 4,000 and can never go over it, but unlike the Valor Points, there is no weekly limit on how much you can earn. In theory, dedicated players can go from 0 to 4,000 in a single day. It is worth noting that whenever a new raid phase is released, all of the Valor Points a player has get converted into JPs, but never over the cap. Additionally, previous Valor Point gear will be converted to costing Justice Points instead and new sets of Valor Point gear will be added.<br/>
<br/>In effect, Justice Points are the "catchup mechanism" for new 85s, being used to purchase catch-up pre-raid gear. In Phase 1, all Justice Point gear is ilvl 346, which means any of these purchases is fairly low-impact - however, it is a good way to shore up any slots where you've been unlucky from dungeon drops.<br/>
<br/>All of these options are listed in no particular order, and are not individually priority to purchase. If you don't have a 346 item in a particular slot and the Justice Point vendor sells an item for that slot, you should buy it.<br/>
<br/>
