<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-holy-paladin-healer">Trinkets for Holy Paladin Healer</h4>T11 trinkets are in a weird place; due to Spirit and Haste being so strong for us, the weights on the top end of trinkets are all very similar. For brevity's sake, we have compressed the list to the top 359 epic trinkets, and then a couple non-359 standout trinkets.<br/>
<br/>Be aware that most 346 trinkets are very poor, and so only a top couple are listed. Every other one sees a large drop in viability, and overall between the existing 359s and the listed 346s, you should easily be able to obtain a set.<br/>
<br/>As a brief overview:<br/>
<br/>Tsunami - Our best pre-raid option, a massive Int+Spirit statstick which is pretty much our ideal trinket.<br/>Doll - Our second-best pre-raid option, or best if you don't have the money for Tsunami/<wbr/>profession for Stone.<br/>Alch Stone - Very close to Tsunami, overtakes on fights shorter than ~5 minutes<br/>Core of Ripeness - Roughly equal to Alch Stone<br/>Tear of Blood - Very similar to Tsunami in that it's the perfect stat combo we want, just a bit worse due to being a proc so how good it is oscillates slightly depending on how the ICD lines up with fight length. On average, on par with Alch Stone/<wbr/>Core<br/>Witching Hourglass - A bit of a weird one as the haste proc is rough to evaluate within the context of Cataclysm healing. On paper, this trinket is much better than this ranking, but in practice, the haste proc is very hit or miss. Ultimately, we'd recommend this only if you are unable to procure the trinkets above.<br/>Mandala - While on paper decent, the Int proc makes it much worse than it seems. Definitely the worst trinket on this list.<div class="pad"></div>
